WEBVTT

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.050
Jululu...

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.840
She was so fussy that time...

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.510
<i>You really don't want to go inside the compact, do you?</i>

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.040
<i>And you cry if I put you in the stroller...</i>

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.610
<i>Won't you go inside the Rosette Pact for me?</i>

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.790
I wonder if she was being so cranky

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:33.180
because she wanted to stay a baby forever.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.270
I mean...

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.350
When she turned back into a goddess, it meant she'd have to disappear.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.060
<i>Mama! Luv you!</i>

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.390
Jululu.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.680
Your mama's going to save you, you hear?

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.000
Greetings, everyone, and welcome to the Divine Idol Grand Prix final!

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:14.420
We'll now be holding a lottery event to determine the competition order!

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.410
It's finally about to begin-pri.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.600
Will a Divine Idol be chosen from among us?

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.810
We'll save Jululu, no matter what.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.310
Yeah!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.910
It's the Divine Idol Grand Prix final!

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.010
We will now hold a lottery event to determine the competition order!

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.910
And the event is being broadcast live worldwide!

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.570
After a gruelling battle,

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.510
those who have won the right to compete for Divine Idolhood...

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.720
the six teams you see before you!

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.180
SoLaMi SMILE!

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.430
Dressing Pafé!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.730
Garmageddon!

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:31.810
NonSugar!

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.440
Ucchari Big Bangs!

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.630
And last, but not least...

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.440
Tricolore!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.840
Hibiki!

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.450
Hibiki-sama!

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:49.620
Hibiki's off filming a movie she's starring in
called "Guitarist of the Battlefield"...

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.260
I see no need to attend in person.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.300
The drawing event is about to begin.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:05.550
I can leave a simple lottery in the hands of Falulu and Fuwari.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:06.660
Very good.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.690
Hibiki-san, we're ready for you to go on standby!

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.090
I'll be back. I leave it in your hands.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:24.330
Hibiki's put her trust in us, so we'll have to do a good job. Right, Falulu?

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.680
Hmph. Everything will be fine.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.110
O–Oh, I'm sure...

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:32.290
The Grand Prix final will be a tournament battle!

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.000
One block has one fewer battle.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.210
First and second from the right are the red block.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.550
Third and fourth are the blue block.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.390
Fifth and sixth are the green block.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:49.680
As you can see, the red block alone has one fewer round, which would be an advantage.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.890
So we win three times, or possibly twice, we pri-vail!

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.860
And if one of us does win...

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:02.360
We can help Jululu... no, <i>Jewlie</i>!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.340
But before we get into the lottery event,

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:13.750
I'd like to explain the three rules of the Grand Prix final tournament rules.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.210
The first rule:

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.130
New songs are not allowed!

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.140
Huh?

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:32.150
Now my secret plot to blow them away with
a heartfelt and passionate new song is ruined!

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:34.520
Dorothy, relax!

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.270
I guess that means no hidden surprises-usa.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:40.990
But we can still bring in new Making Dramas, right-ucha?

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:44.990
Right on! They didn't say a thing about Making Dramas-kuma.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.950
The second rule:

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.120
Victory is determined by the audience's likes!

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.700
It's like we're in the event, too.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.120
So it's not the goddesses this time?

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.230
The third rule:

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:04.130
The Tournament Winner does not necessarily become a Divine Idol.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.300
What?

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.330
Why not?

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.300
I don't get it.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.130
Hey, what's that?

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.270
A stone statue... I pri-sume?

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:20.040
This statue is encased in diamond.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.850
Within it are the Divine Dress and Divine Heels.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:30.630
And with every round, the power of the performances will create cracks in the diamond according to their might.

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:33.030
To reach the level of Divine Idol,

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.820
both must be freed together simultaneously.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.420
At the time both the Divine Dress and Divine Heels are freed,

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.380
a Divine Idol can be born.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:51.700
So that means that even if you win the tournament,
unless you break all of the diamond...

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.350
You won't become a Divine Idol-usa?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.810
All competitors, please do give your utmost in every performance,

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.770
so as to free the coords within the stone statue.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.690
Diamond is the hardest of all minerals-pri.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.700
To even scratch them is a Herculean task.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.160
Then I guess it's just that cosmically tough to become a Divine Idol.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.120
Hmph, diamond is nothing compared to me.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.920
I shall cleave it in twain with my glamour.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.040
Falulu... I think that's enough.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:25.290
So then, what would happen
if the Divine Dress were <i>not</i> freed?

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.260
Then a Divine Idol will not be born.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:33.930
Then, does that mean we won't be able to help Jululu?

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.510
No way...

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:39.400
I think we might have been taking this too lightly-pri.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.440
Huh?

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:45.360
I'd thought no matter what,
one of us <i>would</i> win and save Jululu.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:49.250
I hadn't even considered that
a Divine Idol might not be born at all.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.110
Gulp.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:54.100
So what happens if one of us doesn't become a Divine Idol?

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:58.040
To tell you the truth, not even I know.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:05.290
However, it's been said that a PriPara branch is fated to experience great downfall, desolation, its esteem in ruins.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:08.580
Desolation... in ruins...

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.210
Hey!

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.550
<i>What's this thing?</i>

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:21.550
Did the Sapanna turn out like that because a Divine Idol wasn't born?

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.940
If the same thing happened in Parajuku...

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.400
We have to pri-vent that at all costs!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:32.100
Aye! We will devote every effort so it doesn't end up like in the Sapanna!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.240
We must focus more than before,
and draw upon deeper reserves of strength!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.460
Perhaps we've taken on quite a perilous challenge.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.460
What that? Is that tasty?

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.420
It's not tasty.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.880
Parajuku PriPara will be worthless-garu!

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.340
PriPara will be worthless.. chanko?

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.260
Don't worry!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:05.730
I mean, the fact that we're all here competing for
Divine Idolhood in Parajuku means we've reached this level!

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.190
We all just have to try our best, same as always!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.860
No, even more than always!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.440
Until there's nothing left in the tank!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.910
A Divine Idol will definitely be born,
and we can save Jululu!

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.170
That's right. There's no turning back now.

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.330
We've all got to give it everything we've got-pri!

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:24.890
Let's do it-chanko!

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.330
We'll blow them out of the cosmos!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.600
We'll refasten our loincloths and kick the tension back up to max!

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.810
Relax!

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.480
You wear loincloth? Me too!

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.470
No, it's an expression!

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.430
Okay, everyone!

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:41.140
Let's do it, everyone!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:45.480
We may not have <i>actual</i> loincloths,
but we can tighten our spirits and give it all we've got!

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.250
Capisce!

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.430
Now then, thank you for waiting!

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:55.820
We will now begin the lottery to determine the competition order!

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.370
And you'll choose using the classic PriPara method:
drawing numbers out of a box!

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.540
Kinda simple, huh?

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:06.820
You will draw in this order.

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:10.840
As per tradition, the teams are in order of weight!

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:11.500
What?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.340
Hey, I'm not that heavy!

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:13.960
I object to that-chanko!
Hey, I'm not that heavy!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.800
Garuru's light-garu!

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:20.510
For Miss Garuru, we calculated with her grown-up form.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.180
Please understand: it is tradition.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.890
Ridiculous.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.560
It's just to determine who draws when.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.290
It's nothing for you all to make such a fuss over.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.710
We'll be recording the bridge-blowing scene soon!

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:35.860
Can we please get everyone checked off before we begin?

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:40.570
Now, Miss Ajimi, representing Ucchari Big Bangs, if you would.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.030
Here's Ponkan! They caught
a terracotta warrior, but where was I?

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:49.230
And-it's Warhol, we warriors hauled the number three spot!

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.570
Please, pri-please, any colour but blue.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:54.570
You said it.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.640
Thanks, but no thanks.

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:57.790
That team's like an oncoming freight train.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:02.180
They claimed their slot in the final round, so they have the most momentum.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.550
They look tough to deal with.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.140
They're in a different genre altogether.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.600
Who know what they could do-garu?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:12.560
Here, Little Curly! Get this one! Let's go to war-hol!

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.190
And... action!

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.680
What did you say? Ucchari Big Bangs did?

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:20.610
Cut!
What did you say? Ucchari Big Bangs did?

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.230
Cut!

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.530
Hibiki-san! That's not the line!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.460
We <i>cannot</i> draw blue!

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.910
Filming is cancelled. I'll go there myself!

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:29.460
Very well.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:37.580
Don't you dare pick a number until I get there!

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.880
Now, then, for the second drawing.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.510
The representative of SoLaMi SMILE, if you would.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.640
Okay!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:44.580
Lala.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.860
The probability of drawing blue is one in five: 20 percent.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:54.300
But the odds of drawing the
advantageous red is two in five: 40 pri-cent.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:55.190
You can do it-pri!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.090
I didn't understand a word of that.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:11:59.690
But capisce!

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.400
Here, take this for luck.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.360
You can do it.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.620
Th–Thanks...

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.830
I'm begging you: any colour but blue-kuma!

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.960
<i>It doesn't matter what I draw, or who we face.</i>

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.950
<i>We have to win!</i>

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.210
<i>Believe in me!</i>

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.890
Okay. This is it.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:33.850
Come on!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.660
SoLaMi SMILE enters the green block.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.870
I was hoping for red, but we're pri-vileged enough that it wasn't blue.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.580
SoLaMi SMILE is in the green block.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.620
So our goal must therefore be...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.900
Green alone!

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:57.470
What are you talking about?
You're at the <i>bottom</i> of the list!

00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:58.340
Huh?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.050
Next, the representative of Garmageddon, if you would.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.390
Garuru will draw! Gonna draw!

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:05.720
Hey, Garuru-chan!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.050
Check it out, yummy okonomiyaki!

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.920
And it's all for you if you trade places with us!

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:11.850
Uh.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:13.430
Then how's about this?

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.450
Ooh! Falulu!

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.400
But no!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:16.610
Then how about this? Or this?

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.950
I'm<i> the one who's going to face Onee-chan.</i>

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.910
<i>No one else can take my green!</i>

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.760
Garuru, won't you change places with me?

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.780
Huh?

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:27.530
Non?

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:32.160
If you do change with us, my celebrity assets can prepare anything you wish.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:32.550
Huh?

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:33.500
What?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.860
I, too have my eyes on the most powerful foe.

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:39.110
Which is to say I wish to face your sister.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.380
Okay. Garuru, pretty please?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.670
Garuru, pay no heed to the peons.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:49.550
Behold: Garuru astride the Chariot shall govern the red hell.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.810
She's saying Garuru's gonna draw red!

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.310
Excuse me?

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.510
I shall cast a devil's curse on ye.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:59.170
Garuru, be bold; be bold, Garuru...

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.410
Meat buns are yummy, yummy meat bunsies!

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.460
What kinda curse is that? Buzz off, you!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.690
Please, Garuru!

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.030
Change places with us!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:08.990
Changing sounds fun! Me too!

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.970
Garuru! Now is your time! Draw!

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:15.950
Yeah. Garuru will draw!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.880
<i>Falulu.</i>

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.830
<i>Garuru's goal.</i>

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.950
Want to fight-garu!

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.930
Please! Any colour but green!

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.800
C'mon, pick blue! Blue, darn it!

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.220
Garuru!

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:38.190
Yippee! It's red! Just like we wanted!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.400
We're safe.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.150
Yes – for now, at least.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:45.070
Well done, Garuru! You truly are the Devil's own unholy one!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.610
Why, this portends nothing but...

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.840
Garmageddon's certain victory!

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.900
You sure do get carried away, Aroma!

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:55.290
We're the tightest-knit of them all-nekon!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:01.210
Let us make it in time. I <i>must</i> draw myself!

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:06.920
Each block now has one team entered: red, blue and green.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:11.890
Each draw from now on will determine that team's opponent.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.920
Okay, and that means I'm next!

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.330
Me draw!

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.090
No, this is a task for a celebrity.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.100
Wait up!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.100
Gonna be me!

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.230
It shall be I!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.140
Gonna be me!

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:23.020
Shall be I!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.060
Hey!

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.860
Both of you, prostrate yourselves and capisce!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.660
<i>I have to draw green, the same as Onee-chan.</i>

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:32.740
<i>It has to be green!</i>

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:38.720
Hey, there! Didja know there's one ball of each: red, blue and green?

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.580
Now, I wonder just which one she'll choose!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.920
Will she draw blue, and be up against Ucchari?

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.440
Or green, and we'll see a battle of the sisters?

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.420
Or will it be Garmageddon after all?

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:51.040
<i>Which ball is green? Green for Onee-chan?</i>

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.390
Now, choose! Which will it be?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.830
<i>I have to draw green.</i>

00:15:56.830 --> 00:16:00.600
<i>No matter what, I have to face Onee-chan!</i>

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:05.810
All right! It's green!

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:19.620
Onee-chan, it's time to accept the next era of PriPara –
led by us, the new generation!

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:24.960
Oho, someone here pri-sumes drawing the lot is the same as winning.

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.420
I hear you, Non, loud and clear.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:29.420
But I'm not planning to lose either.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.840
Hey, no, scratch all of that!

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.430
Dorothy, relax...
We're the ones who're gonna fight SoLaMi SMILE, darn it!

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.430
Hey, are we still not there?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:39.780
We'll arrive shortly.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.640
Hurry! Hurry, I say!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:44.310
Don't you dare draw before I arrive!

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:46.170
Now, then – next is...

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:03.330
Halt this ball-drawing!

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.710
Hey, is that Hibiki-san?

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.450
<i>I</i> will draw!

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:14.300
Oh, but...

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:19.510
I already did...

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:21.680
<i>B–Blue!</i>

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.080
I'm sorry, Hibiki-san.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.610
What are you apologising for?

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:36.320
Any result from your draw is the best choice.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.950
Oh, I'm so glad.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:41.990
Now Tricolore is in the blue block.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:46.860
Which means Dressing Pafé automatically enters the red block.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.220
So, what, we're up against Garmageddon?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:52.420
This'll be a cinch!

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:53.630
Garu!

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.000
<i>Ouch</i>!

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:58.970
That's no play-bite – she's just tryin' to hurt me!

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:01.870
Lemme go, ya little...

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:07.100
The first battle in round one will be the red block:
Garmageddon and Dressing Pafé.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:12.610
Now, as today marks the eve of the tournament beginning tomorrow, I think a celebratory performance is in order.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.820
Which team shall we ask to perform?

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:15.560
It's gotta be us!

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.700
We shall claim the dishonour!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.400
Yep!

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.450
We wanna do it!

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.780
I'd love to do it!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.240
Dosukoi!

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.200
What?

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:31.380
No one celebrates as cosmically as we can!

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:32.210
Chanko!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.420
Da Vinci!

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.490
What?

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:36.380
They bargeded on in!

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.550
Blow us away!

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.900
Making Drama, switch on!

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.910
Cosmic!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.870
Whirly-whirly-whirly-whirly!

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:31.160
Whirly-whi-Rubens!

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:32.910
Dosukoi!

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.670
Chanko!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:38.210
Da Vinci!
Cosmic!

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.920
All on the line!

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.060
Bare-knuckled Pri-me Donne!

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:44.180
Da Vinci!

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:47.260
Mystery Cyalume Change!

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:54.480
Chanko!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:55.400
Cosmic!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.100
Da Vinci!

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:25.430
Thank you for this blessing!

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:26.820
I love you, Chanko!

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:28.680
Cosmo-san, you're out of the cosmos!

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:30.100
Ajimi-chan, where'd you go?

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:37.310
One week from today, the last round of the Grand Prix final will be held.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:40.380
The venue for our competition... is here!

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:44.950
Here we go!

00:21:54.230 --> 00:21:56.160
It's the atrium stage-pri...

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:59.260
Welcome to the final stage.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:03.170
Jewlie! Janice!

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:08.890
I look forward to seeing you all in the first round of the tournament next week!

00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:15.180
So it's finally starting.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:18.060
The Divine Idol Grand Prix Final.

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:18.850
Yeah.

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:57.790
Devil, angel and beast are combined:
the night to unleash our final form is come!

00:23:57.790 --> 00:24:00.490
Garmageddon will rain blessings upon everyone!

00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:02.350
Garuru will bite! Until I win!

00:24:02.350 --> 00:24:03.670
A headlong dash!

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:06.070
Our only path leads to victory and Divine Idolhood!

00:24:06.070 --> 00:24:09.370
You little babies can sit back
and see some grown-up spice!

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:13.260
We'll always be together –
because we're Dressing Pafé!

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:16.810
Next time, <i>Rocking Gajira Climactic Battle</i>!

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:20.060
Aim to be a Divine Idol! Let's go, PriPara!
